<!--
     Single-colour layer for themed launcher icons. The system supplies the
     tint, so this must be one flat shape with the glyph knocked out.

     Calculator, replacing the shield on 2026-08-08 — see
     ic_launcher_foreground.xml for why, and for the 44x56-on-(54,54) geometry
     that keeps it inside the Wear launcher's circular mask.

     ONE PATH, evenOdd. The body is the ink; the screen and the six keys are
     subpaths that punch through it. What survives is the body outline plus the
     gutters between the keys, which is what makes this read as a calculator
     rather than as a filled rectangle — a themed icon gets no second colour to
     carry the detail, so the negative space has to do it.

     Deliberately NOT the readout bar from the colour layer: at one tint it
     would merge with the screen cutout and only thicken an edge.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M38,26h32a6,6 0 0 1 6,6v44a6,6 0 0 1 -6,6h-32a6,6 0 0 1 -6,-6v-44a6,6 0 0 1 6,-6zM38,32h32v14h-32zM38,54h8v10h-8zM50,54h8v10h-8zM62,54h8v10h-8zM38,68h8v10h-8zM50,68h8v10h-8zM62,68h8v10h-8z" />
